## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js (App Router) project.

### Changes Made

1. **Installed Package**
   - Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` to dependencies using npm
   - Updated package.json and package-lock.json

2. **Modified Files**
   - `app/layout.tsx`: Added Analytics component following official Vercel documentation
     - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
     - Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body tag

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Analytics component is placed in the root layout file (`app/layout.tsx`)
- Component is positioned at the end of the `<body>` tag after the existing providers
- This ensures analytics tracking is enabled across all pages in the application

### Verification

✅ Build completed successfully with no errors
✅ Linting passed for the modified layout.tsx file
✅ TypeScript compilation successful
✅ No breaking changes introduced to existing functionality

### Next Steps

To complete the setup:
1. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. Deploy the application to Vercel
3. Verify analytics data collection by checking the browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view`

The analytics will automatically start tracking page views once the application is deployed on Vercel.
